## 📄 Summary Notes

- File system = structure for storing and organizing data.
- NTFS = supports permissions, ADS, encryption.
- Weak permissions allow attackers to move laterally or plant malware.
- ADS = hidden data streams inside files.
- Attackers hide payloads to avoid detection.
- PowerShell = powerful Windows automation + attacker tool.
- Fileless malware uses PowerShell in memory.
- Lateral movement = moving through network.
- Persistence = staying after reboot.

